## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of temporal, multi-step constraints in a 3-valued logic setting. Requires constructing a concrete model and outlining a backtracking propagator that preserves non-F constraints while allowing Unknowns.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued semantics for implication
- Temporal constraint propagation across time steps
- Unit/branching propagation in backtracking

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: evaluateImp(A,B) returns Kleene(A,B)
function evaluateImp(A,B){ // A,B in {T,F,U}
  // ¬A ∨ B with Kleene ordering T>U>F
  const not = {T:'F', F:'T', U:'U'}[A];
  const order = { 'F':0, 'U':1, 'T':2 };
  // ⩒ is max by value order
  const values = [not, B];
  let best = 'F';
  for (const v of values) if (order[v] > order[best]) best = v;
  return best;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests temporal extension of 3-valued reasoning with forward/backward propagation and fixed-point thinking.

## Key Concepts
- Temporal 3-valued logic with Kleene semantics
- Implication as ¬A ∨ B across time slices
- Forward-chaining propagated to fixed point

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagate(states, rules){
  let changed=true;
  while(changed){
    changed=false;
    for(const r of rules){
      const a = evalExpr(r.ante, states);
      const b = evalExpr(r.cons, states);
      const out = imp(a,b); // Kleene A→B
      if(states[r.target] !== out){ states[r.target] = out; changed=true; }
    }
  }
  return states;
}
```

